<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">University of Vienna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1365–present</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> was founded in 1365 by Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolf-iv-duke-of-austria">Rudolf IV of Austria</a> and is the oldest university in today's German-speaking world. A papal bull approved most faculties at the start, and a faculty of theology was added in 1384. It became one of the largest universities in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and a centre of medicine, philosophy and science.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/university-of-vienna.jpg" alt="University of Vienna" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Universität Wien Vector: Lệ Xuân · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seal_of_the_University_of_Vienna.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
